# Build outputs — anything produced by ./tools/build_userspace.sh or
# ./vnu/build_iso.sh must be ignored, not committed. If a build step starts
# producing a new artifact, add it here (see AGENTS.md).

# Kernel CMake build tree
vnu/kernel/build/

# Staged ISO payload and final image (the whole staging dir is generated)
vnu/iso/
vnu/vnu.iso

# GRUB boot blobs extracted from a grub-mkrescue ISO for the portable
# (xorriso-only) ISO builder used on hosts without grub tools (Termux).
vnu/grub-seed/

# Scratch dir used while regenerating the grub-seed (grub-mkrescue temp)
vnu/.tmp_grub/

# Compiled userspace ELFs + the vcc sysroot (headers are mirrors of
# vlibc/include) and the kernel .bss blobs embedded from them
sysroot/
vnu/kernel/proc/embedded_*.h

# Generic object/archive debris
*.o
*.iso

# Test disk image produced by ./vnu/run.sh vhd
vnu/vnu.vhd
# Python bytecode from importing tools/qemu_test.py (a probe script or an
# IDE indexer drops this next to the harness)
__pycache__/

# ROADMAP.md is my own working plan for what comes next, together with the
# churn rule that goes with it (declined work is deleted from it, not parked
# in it). Deliberately not part of the tree: a plan that lives in the
# repository is a promise to reviewers and a source of stale entries, and
# mine is neither. Do not "fix" this line — if it ever belongs in the tree,
# translate it to English first (AGENTS.md) and commit it on purpose.
ROADMAP.md

# The switch `make thamoff` throws: an image built without the third-party
# modules in thams/ is a deliberate build, not a leftover. Local to one
# tree, so it is never committed.
thams/.off
